  "id": "bihugeet",
  "name": "Bihu geet (Assamese spring-festival song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bihu geet are the songs of Rongali (Bohag) Bihu, the Assamese spring new-year festival, sung at open-air bihu dances and by husori groups who go from house to house. The ensemble centres on the double-headed dhol with the pepa buffalo-horn pipe, the gogona bamboo jaw harp, taal cymbals and bamboo flute; the kubing card, a bamboo jaw harp, stands in for the bamboo gogona, the manjira card for the taal and the flute card for the baanhi; the pepa is not given a card here.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bihu geet, carnival Processional, south Asian branch. live take. dhol, bamboo credited bamboo flute unspecified, kubing, manjira. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
